{"slug": "vodka-sauce", "nyt_id": 787865328, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/787865328-vodka-sauce", "name": "Vodka Sauce", "author": "Dan Pelosi", "description": "This vodka sauce recipe, adapted from my cookbook “Let’s Eat” (Union Square & Co., 2023), leans into the creamier, glossier side of this traditional Italian sauce. It avoids using alliums like shallot or onion or salty meats like bacon or pancetta at the start of the recipe, instead focusing on whisking up a smooth sauce that highlights the famously sweet and tangy flavor that results from cooking the alcohol out of the vodka. While most traditionally used on pasta, this sauce also brings new life to chicken Parmesan or pizza. It is easily made vegan with the use of non-dairy cream substitutes, and comes back to life as leftovers by adding just a splash or two of pasta water while reheating.", "servings": {"text": "4-6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 10, "cook_minutes": 40, "total_minutes": 50, "raw": {"total": "50 min", "prep": "PT0H10M", "cook": "PT0H40M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "Kosher salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ cup extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons unsalted butter", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "unsalted butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Crushed red pepper (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "crushed red pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 5, "raw": "3 garlic cloves, grated", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "grated", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "6 tablespoons tomato paste", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "tomato paste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 pound rigatoni", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "rigatoni", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 pint heavy cream", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "pint", "item": "heavy cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "6 tablespoons vodka", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "vodka", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "Freshly grated Parmesan or pecorino cheese, for serving", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly grated parmesan or pecorino cheese", "preparation": "for serving", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil over high heat."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Meanwhile, in a large skillet over medium heat, combine the olive oil, butter and a pinch of crushed red pepper (if using). Cook, whisking to blend the fats together while the butter is melting. Add the garlic and tomato paste. Whisk until the tomato paste is deep red, 3 to 5 minutes."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Add the rigatoni to the boiling water and cook until al dente according to the package directions. Reserve 1 cup of the pasta cooking water, then drain and set aside."}, {"position": 4, "text": "As soon as the pasta hits the water, add the heavy cream to the skillet and continue whisking until the cream is fully incorporated and the sauce color darkens slightly, about 5 minutes. Add the vodka to the sauce and cook, continuing to whisk, until the alcohol cooks out (the strong scent of the vodka will disappear), and the sauce is perfectly smooth, about 5 minutes more."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Add ½ cup of the reserved pasta water to the sauce. Continue to simmer and whisk frequently until the sauce is thick enough to coat the back of a spoon without sliding off, 15 to 20 minutes."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Add the cooked pasta to the sauce and stir until coated and glossy. Divide among plates, top with Parmesan, and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 809.2, "protein_g": 14.4, "carbohydrates_g": 62.4, "fat_g": 53.0, "saturated_fat_g": 24.2, "trans_fat_g": 1.0, "cholesterol_mg": 104.8, "sodium_mg": 497.3, "fiber_g": 3.1, "sugar_g": 6.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 25.7, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian american"], "diet": ["egg-free", "peanut-free", "tree nut-free", "soy-free", "fish-free", "shellfish-free", "pork-free", "sesame-free", "vegetarian", "pescatarian"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["heavy cream", "rigatoni", "tomato paste", "vodka", "sauces and gravies", "simmer", "easy", "quick", "weeknight", "pastas", "great leftovers", "creator"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/08/28/multimedia/DP-Vodka-Sauce-gjvc/DP-Vodka-Sauce-gjvc-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 61}, "video_url": "https://www.nytimes.com/video/embedded/dining/100000011077653/vodka-sauce.html", "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2026-08-28", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:28:32.840370+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "vodka-sauce-tomato-soup", "nyt_id": 769631925, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/769631925-vodka-sauce-tomato-soup", "name": "Vodka Sauce Tomato Soup", "author": "Ella Quittner", "description": "This soup, from my cookbook “Obsessed With the Best” (HarperCollins, 2026), relies on a layering of flavor from roasting both fresh and canned tomatoes, which each have different levels of sweetness, acidity and tomato-to-water concentrations. Then, a sort of vodka sauce approach enters the picture and contributes bisque-adjacent richness and spice. It’s excellent on its own, or with a grilled cheese sandwich (ideally American cheese between soft slices of white bread or milk bread) or topped with crumbled crackers that soften over the top as you eat.", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": null, "raw": {}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 (28-ounce) can crushed tomatoes and their juices", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "(28-ounce) can crushed tomatoes and their juices", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 pints cherry tomatoes", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "pint", "item": "cherry tomatoes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "¼ cup plus 2 tablespoons olive oil, divided", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "plus 2 tablespoons olive oil", "preparation": "divided", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 teaspoons kosher salt, such as Diamond Crystal, plus more as needed", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": "such as Diamond Crystal, plus more as needed", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "½ teaspoon freshly cracked black pepper, plus more as needed", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "freshly cracked black pepper", "preparation": "plus more as needed", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "3 tablespoons unsalted butter", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "unsalted butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 yellow onion, diced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "yellow onion", "preparation": "diced", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "4 garlic cloves, roughly smashed and peeled", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "roughly smashed and peeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "½ cup double-concentrated tomato paste, about 1 (4 ½-ounce) tube", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "double-concentrated tomato paste", "preparation": "about 1 (4 ½-ounce) tube", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "3 jarred Calabrian chiles, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "jarred calabrian chiles", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "½ cup vodka", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "vodka", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 cup heavy cream", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "heavy cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "Fresh basil leaves, for serving", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "fresh basil leaves", "preparation": "for serving", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat the oven to 375 degrees. Spread the canned crushed tomatoes and the cherry tomatoes in a small roasting pan (like an 8-by-8-inch baking pan or a quarter sheet pan) with ¼ cup oil, the salt and pepper. Roast for about 1 hour, until the cherry tomatoes are tender and sweet and the canned crushed tomatoes have gone jammy and dark red, with the oil floating at the top."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Meanwhile, heat the remaining 2 tablespoons oil in a Dutch oven over medium-low heat. Melt the butter in the oil, then add the onion and garlic and sauté for about 20 minutes, until softened and beginning to caramelize around the edges."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Make a well in the center of the onion mixture and add the tomato paste. Cook for about 4 minutes, stirring frequently, until darkened and fragrant and sticking to the bottom and sides of the pan. Add the Calabrian chiles and deglaze the pan with the vodka, stirring to combine and release any browned bits."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Add the oven-roasted tomatoes and all their juices from the baking pan, scraping in any sticky bits. Stir in the cream and 3 cups of water. Cook at a low but sprightly simmer for 25 to 30 minutes, until the soup is thick and deeply flavored. (You can cook it for longer if you like an extra-thick soup.)"}, {"position": 5, "text": "Use an immersion blender to make it as smooth as you like, and season with more salt and pepper to taste."}, {"position": 6, "text": "When ready to serve, thinly slice a few basil leaves to sprinkle over the top of each bowl of soup."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 674.5, "protein_g": 9.2, "carbohydrates_g": 36.1, "fat_g": 51.6, "saturated_fat_g": 22.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": null, "trans_fat_g": 0.7, "cholesterol_mg": 90.1, "sodium_mg": 1376.7, "fiber_g": 8.4, "sugar_g": 22.1, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving"}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian american inspired"], "diet": ["vegetarian", "gluten-free"], "course": ["appetizer", "main course"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["cherry tomato", "crushed canned tomato", "vodka", "soup", "lunch", "dinner", "simmer", "winter", "fall", "tomato paste", "heavy cream", "vegetables", "roast"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/02/02/multimedia/EQ-Vodka-Sauce-Tomato-Soup-bcwj/EQ-Vodka-Sauce-Tomato-Soup-bcwj-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 287}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2026-02-02", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T11:59:44.424293+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
